From: op15-gki-kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] mm: page_alloc: disable default watermark_boost_factor

Mainline's watermark_boost_factor = 15000 triggers aggressive kswapd
reclaim spikes after bursty high-order graphics and camera allocations.
Default watermark_boost_factor to 0 on mobile while keeping the sysctl
tunable at runtime.
---
diff --git a/mm/page_alloc.c b/mm/page_alloc.c
index 7a1149f..3b06b42 100644
--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -349,7 +349,7 @@ const char * const migratetype_names[MIGRATE_TYPES] = {
 
 int min_free_kbytes = 1024;
 int user_min_free_kbytes = -1;
-static int watermark_boost_factor __read_mostly = 15000;
+static int watermark_boost_factor __read_mostly;
 static int watermark_scale_factor = 10;
 
 /* movable_zone is the "real" zone pages in ZONE_MOVABLE are taken from */
